{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:418812d15e0c07e3","name":"Improved Force Lightning","source":{"id":"source:reference-418812d15e0c07e3","title":"Improved Force Lightning","revision":19483,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:03:27Z","sha256":"f4a826af0308ea31b1ed6d8ed4e447999d14fab917f306f9d8808962c1bc6336","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19483","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Improved%20Force%20Lightning&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-418812d15e0c07e3","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When you use the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Lightning"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Lightning","referenceId":"reference:a654f003ddc04a24"}]}," Force Power, you can choose to change the time it takes to activate to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},". If you do, your target must make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," check. If your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check result beats the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," check, you push the target back 1 square plus 1 additional square for every 5 points by which you exceed the target's check result. If you push the target into a larger object, the target takes 1d6 points of damage.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The target adds its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," and size modifier to its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," check: Colossal, +20; Gargantuan, +15; Huge, +10; Large, +5; Medium, +0; Small, -5; Tiny, -10; Diminutive, -15; Fine, -20. In addition, the target gets a +5 stability bonus if it has more than two legs or is otherwise exceptionally stable.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
